1
00:00:07,174 --> 00:00:10,677
[sensual music]

2
00:00:17,601 --> 00:00:19,144
[moans]

3
00:00:23,440 --> 00:00:25,442
[sensual music continues]

4
00:00:32,866 --> 00:00:34,868
[moans]

5
00:00:37,996 --> 00:00:40,374
Does it have to be from behind?

6
00:00:42,876 --> 00:00:43,877
[Elisse] Andrea.

7
00:00:44,127 --> 00:00:45,587
Elisse! Um...

8
00:00:45,671 --> 00:00:47,756
Sorry. Uh, no, uh...

9
00:00:47,839 --> 00:00:51,134
I just received these rushes.

10
00:00:51,218 --> 00:00:52,469
There's a complaint from a talent.

11
00:00:52,553 --> 00:00:54,721
So I had to check her poses.

12
00:00:54,805 --> 00:00:57,558
Her hip was aching.
So, I just... You know.

13
00:00:57,641 --> 00:00:59,393
- What can I do for you?
- Mmm...

14
00:01:03,313 --> 00:01:04,356
SAM.

15
00:01:05,315 --> 00:01:07,442
- Oh.
- [Elisse] I want to talk about SAM.

16
00:01:11,822 --> 00:01:12,948
Okay.

17
00:01:13,824 --> 00:01:15,909
[in English]
I just really want to spend

18
00:01:16,451 --> 00:01:18,620
as much time as I can with Felize.

19
00:01:19,871 --> 00:01:21,707
[in Filipino] I want to...

20
00:01:21,790 --> 00:01:22,791
[clicks tongue]

21
00:01:23,333 --> 00:01:25,127
I want to...

22
00:01:26,128 --> 00:01:28,422
cut down on my workload.

23
00:01:29,590 --> 00:01:30,632
I'm sorry.

24
00:01:31,133 --> 00:01:32,134
I've decided that

25
00:01:32,467 --> 00:01:33,844
this is how it should be.

26
00:01:34,970 --> 00:01:37,139
Of course, I understand you. Come on.

27
00:01:37,639 --> 00:01:39,725
But what about your income?

28
00:01:40,517 --> 00:01:43,353
Well, I'm not really...

29
00:01:44,229 --> 00:01:46,106
quitting, no.

30
00:01:46,356 --> 00:01:47,399
- [Andrea] Okay.
- But...

31
00:01:47,858 --> 00:01:50,527
I'm gonna have to be more picky.

32
00:01:50,611 --> 00:01:52,738
- I'll say "no" to some projects.
- Mm-hm.

33
00:01:54,948 --> 00:01:56,992
Like... I'm passing on
Juan Makabayan.

34
00:01:57,075 --> 00:01:58,243
I won't do it anymore.

35
00:01:59,745 --> 00:02:03,749
Actually, I think that, maybe,
this is not a good time

36
00:02:04,041 --> 00:02:05,876
especially since SAM's closing down.

37
00:02:06,793 --> 00:02:09,463
[playful music]

38
00:02:09,546 --> 00:02:10,756
Hm...

39
00:02:18,889 --> 00:02:21,683
Oh, my god, Deo. Oh, I'm sorry.

40
00:02:21,767 --> 00:02:23,352
Deo, this is the absolute worst.

41
00:02:24,269 --> 00:02:26,647
Chin, how was the Portrait shoot?

42
00:02:27,272 --> 00:02:29,441
- Why?
- I'll report to Ms. Andrea.

43
00:02:29,524 --> 00:02:30,901
Of course you will.

44
00:02:30,984 --> 00:02:32,319
I was there until dawn

45
00:02:32,402 --> 00:02:35,155
because Maricel and Snooky
did nothing but bicker.

46
00:02:35,238 --> 00:02:37,407
One refused to go to the set

47
00:02:37,491 --> 00:02:39,826
and the other wanted to go home.

48
00:02:40,994 --> 00:02:41,995
Really?

49
00:02:42,871 --> 00:02:44,748
They were okay when I was there.

50
00:02:45,791 --> 00:02:46,792
Are you saying it's my fault?

51
00:02:47,209 --> 00:02:48,293
That I can't control them?

52
00:02:48,377 --> 00:02:49,711
No, I don't mean it that way.

53
00:02:50,337 --> 00:02:52,506
Do you have a problem with me?
Have I done something?

54
00:02:52,964 --> 00:02:54,883
Why would I have a problem with you?

55
00:02:56,093 --> 00:02:57,260
[Sofie] Camille.

56
00:02:57,636 --> 00:02:59,262
Let me through.

57
00:02:59,346 --> 00:03:01,473
Ms. Andrea says

58
00:03:01,556 --> 00:03:03,266
she needs to talk to you later.

59
00:03:03,350 --> 00:03:05,352
And Sir Matthew told me

60
00:03:05,769 --> 00:03:08,939
to tell you to help Noemi

61
00:03:09,022 --> 00:03:11,400
with the documents for the meeting
with Ms. Helen.

62
00:03:11,900 --> 00:03:12,901
Okay.

63
00:03:17,239 --> 00:03:18,240
Okay.

64
00:03:18,323 --> 00:03:19,658
It seems like I'm not needed here.

65
00:03:19,741 --> 00:03:20,992
Maybe I can go home and rest.

66
00:03:22,953 --> 00:03:25,330
Or is there anything else I need
to report to you, Ms. Camille?

67
00:03:30,377 --> 00:03:31,503
What was that about?

68
00:03:32,462 --> 00:03:35,132
[cell phone ringing]

69
00:03:42,013 --> 00:03:43,014
[Chin] Sorry.

70
00:03:45,517 --> 00:03:46,977
Hello.

71
00:03:47,519 --> 00:03:49,438
Didn't I say that I'd call?

72
00:03:49,938 --> 00:03:52,858
I just wanted to commend
your good work, and...

73
00:03:52,941 --> 00:03:55,318
Maybe you can ramp it up a bit more?

74
00:03:55,402 --> 00:03:56,653
Make it a little bit faster.

75
00:03:57,320 --> 00:03:58,363
What?

76
00:03:59,072 --> 00:04:01,825
Sir, you know how tough it is
keeping our secret.

77
00:04:01,908 --> 00:04:04,286
[Paul over phone]
Yes, but that promotion I'm offering

78
00:04:04,369 --> 00:04:06,246
should get you all fired up.

79
00:04:06,329 --> 00:04:07,914
- [Joseph] Oh!
- Hi, Joseph!

80
00:04:07,998 --> 00:04:10,250
What's up?
What are you doing? Loitering again?

81
00:04:15,839 --> 00:04:18,300
Look, I'll see what I can do, sir.

82
00:04:18,383 --> 00:04:21,553
Your agency is on its way down!

83
00:04:22,012 --> 00:04:25,432
I'm sure you've heard
about Matthew's daughter, right?

84
00:04:25,515 --> 00:04:27,392
I have, sir.

85
00:04:27,476 --> 00:04:30,312
See that? If you don't move on,
they're going to take you

86
00:04:30,395 --> 00:04:31,438
down with them.

87
00:04:31,521 --> 00:04:32,564
You don't want that, do you?

88
00:04:32,647 --> 00:04:35,150
[Paul over phone]
Do you know who's the first

89
00:04:35,233 --> 00:04:37,027
celebrity you're going to manage

90
00:04:37,110 --> 00:04:38,695
when you sign up with us is?

91
00:04:40,238 --> 00:04:41,698
Roderick Paulate.

92
00:04:42,157 --> 00:04:44,659
The Box Office King! See?

93
00:04:44,743 --> 00:04:47,078
Let me show you just how Galaxy works

94
00:04:47,162 --> 00:04:48,663
how we manage our stars

95
00:04:48,747 --> 00:04:51,208
how we make the most
out of every situation

96
00:04:51,291 --> 00:04:53,627
so we can get the best out of them.

97
00:04:53,710 --> 00:04:54,753
You'll see.

98
00:04:54,836 --> 00:04:58,548
I don't care about the private lives
of these celebrities.

99
00:04:58,632 --> 00:05:02,677
I don't even care that they're
a bunch of stupid divas in real life.

100
00:05:03,345 --> 00:05:06,389
As long as they bring in the money,
then I will love them.

101
00:05:06,473 --> 00:05:07,641
I will take care of them

102
00:05:07,724 --> 00:05:09,976
and we will make the most
out of them.

103
00:05:10,060 --> 00:05:13,230
But the moment they fail to deliver,
then it's goodbye.

104
00:05:13,313 --> 00:05:14,314
It's goodbye.

105
00:05:14,397 --> 00:05:15,607
And you know what you call that?

106
00:05:16,316 --> 00:05:18,693
You call that good business.

107
00:05:19,236 --> 00:05:21,279
That's a little harsh,
don't you think?

108
00:05:21,363 --> 00:05:22,697
Are you with me?

109
00:05:22,781 --> 00:05:25,075
Okay, sir, but I have to go. Bye!

110
00:05:28,245 --> 00:05:29,246
My god.

111
00:05:29,496 --> 00:05:31,498
[theme music]

112
00:05:33,583 --> 00:05:35,710
♪ Careful, careful ♪

113
00:05:36,753 --> 00:05:39,339
♪ The world is full
Of jealous people ♪

114
00:05:39,631 --> 00:05:42,676
♪ When envy strikes,
It means trouble ♪

115
00:05:42,926 --> 00:05:45,011
♪ That's why we need to be careful ♪

116
00:05:45,095 --> 00:05:47,556
♪ Careful, careful ♪

117
00:05:48,223 --> 00:05:51,142
♪ We always need to be careful ♪

118
00:05:51,560 --> 00:05:54,145
♪ Prying eyes ready to snoop ♪

119
00:05:54,604 --> 00:05:57,482
♪ Digging for the juiciest scoop ♪

120
00:05:57,566 --> 00:05:59,818
♪ That's why we need to be careful ♪

121
00:06:03,196 --> 00:06:05,574
♪ Careful, careful ♪

122
00:06:08,159 --> 00:06:11,204
Eventually, Maricel and Snooky
got back to work

123
00:06:11,288 --> 00:06:13,582
and finished all their
scheduled scenes for today.

124
00:06:13,665 --> 00:06:15,125
[Andrea] Yeah,
and what about Zsa Zsa?

125
00:06:16,167 --> 00:06:17,627
I heard she's leaving us.

126
00:06:18,086 --> 00:06:19,838
You know already? That was fast.

127
00:06:20,088 --> 00:06:21,381
So you told your dad?

128
00:06:22,048 --> 00:06:23,592
It was Noemi who told him.

129
00:06:25,218 --> 00:06:26,386
Another news.

130
00:06:27,470 --> 00:06:29,723
Elisse is cutting back on work.

131
00:06:29,806 --> 00:06:31,933
She's away from her kid too long.

132
00:06:33,226 --> 00:06:36,855
So now I bet everyone thinks
all my talents are problematic.

133
00:06:37,439 --> 00:06:39,858
I tried my best with Ms. Zsa Zsa.

134
00:06:40,483 --> 00:06:42,319
Maybe you didn't explain it well.

135
00:06:42,736 --> 00:06:45,947
[Andrea] In the first place,
you're always working with Karylle

136
00:06:46,031 --> 00:06:47,282
but you still haven't fixed this?

137
00:06:48,158 --> 00:06:49,451
May I remind you

138
00:06:50,619 --> 00:06:52,120
that I'm the one who hired you.

139
00:06:53,038 --> 00:06:56,291
Prove to me that I made
the right decision in hiring you.

140
00:06:57,208 --> 00:06:59,002
And again, you work for me.

141
00:06:59,377 --> 00:07:01,546
Not for Matthew, for me.

142
00:07:01,630 --> 00:07:02,631
Yes, ma'am.

143
00:07:03,006 --> 00:07:04,466
Now, if you really want

144
00:07:04,549 --> 00:07:06,801
the junior manager position,
then do your job.

145
00:07:07,052 --> 00:07:08,762
Fix the Karylle and Zsa Zsa thing.

146
00:07:08,845 --> 00:07:10,680
- You heard me?
- Yes, Ms. Andrea.

147
00:07:10,764 --> 00:07:12,515
Okay. My script.

148
00:07:14,809 --> 00:07:15,810
Go.

149
00:07:21,191 --> 00:07:23,360
[inquisitive music]

150
00:07:23,443 --> 00:07:26,404
Sorry! Sorry.

151
00:07:32,452 --> 00:07:34,287
Do you need anything, Noemi?

152
00:07:34,371 --> 00:07:36,915
No. Just go on.

153
00:07:43,296 --> 00:07:45,799
- [awkward chuckle]
- Wha... Why?

154
00:07:46,216 --> 00:07:47,592
Who are you messaging?

155
00:07:47,676 --> 00:07:49,719
- Karylle.
- Aah...

156
00:07:49,803 --> 00:07:51,096
Just Karylle? No one else?

157
00:07:51,763 --> 00:07:53,348
I mean, why?

158
00:07:53,890 --> 00:07:57,477
Ms. Andrea told me to find a way
for Karylle and her mom to make up.

159
00:07:58,103 --> 00:08:00,146
- Is there something wrong?
- No, nothing's wrong!

160
00:08:02,524 --> 00:08:05,318
Nothing. Thanks!

161
00:08:06,111 --> 00:08:07,237
Thanks!

162
00:08:11,116 --> 00:08:14,953
[inquisitive music]

163
00:08:35,557 --> 00:08:37,434
- [Chin] Did someone text me?
- [Noemi gasps]

164
00:08:41,312 --> 00:08:43,273
[cell phone ringing]

165
00:08:44,149 --> 00:08:47,193
Hello, yes, Sir Gab. Mm-hm.

166
00:08:47,277 --> 00:08:49,362
I'm in the pantry. Okay, on my way.

167
00:08:50,530 --> 00:08:51,740
- Later, Noemi.
- Mm!

168
00:09:07,047 --> 00:09:09,174
[cell phone pinging]

169
00:09:13,303 --> 00:09:16,014
[tense music]

170
00:09:21,186 --> 00:09:23,605
[cell phone pinging]

171
00:09:27,108 --> 00:09:28,109
Need anything?

172
00:09:34,657 --> 00:09:36,951
[tense music intensifies]

173
00:09:39,871 --> 00:09:42,123
[inaudible dialogue]

174
00:09:48,880 --> 00:09:52,300
[inaudible dialogue]

175
00:10:00,266 --> 00:10:03,770
[Noemi shrieks]

176
00:10:04,938 --> 00:10:06,272
- What happened?
- What was that?

177
00:10:11,194 --> 00:10:12,237
Excuse me.

178
00:10:13,279 --> 00:10:14,280
What was that?

179
00:10:17,659 --> 00:10:18,743
What happened?

180
00:10:18,827 --> 00:10:19,953
- Are you okay?
- Uh...

181
00:10:20,286 --> 00:10:21,287
[awkward chuckle]

182
00:10:21,371 --> 00:10:23,248
Sorry, I thought
there was a cockroach.

183
00:10:23,790 --> 00:10:24,874
[all] Huh?

184
00:10:26,459 --> 00:10:28,128
- What a waste of time.
- You're weird.

185
00:10:28,211 --> 00:10:29,212
What a huge cockroach!

186
00:10:31,422 --> 00:10:33,007
Are you okay?

187
00:10:33,341 --> 00:10:34,342
[Noemi] Yeah.

188
00:10:34,425 --> 00:10:36,970
That was some scream.
We heard you all the way here!

189
00:10:37,053 --> 00:10:38,555
It sounded like murder.

190
00:10:38,638 --> 00:10:41,307
I thought there was
a flying cockroach.

191
00:10:41,766 --> 00:10:43,518
- A cockroach?
- It's just a pin.

192
00:10:43,768 --> 00:10:45,436
How can that look like a cockroach?

193
00:10:45,520 --> 00:10:48,022
I'm not sure, I'm not really sure.

194
00:10:48,565 --> 00:10:50,024
- Hey, Sofie?
- Yeah?

195
00:10:50,108 --> 00:10:52,068
Can you put everything here?

196
00:10:52,152 --> 00:10:54,154
Ogie Diaz's videos

197
00:10:54,487 --> 00:10:58,074
the leaked stories about Brandon
and about Rob.

198
00:10:59,367 --> 00:11:00,660
There's more.

199
00:11:01,494 --> 00:11:02,996
[Sofie] Now everyone knows

200
00:11:03,079 --> 00:11:06,416
about Ms. Zsa Zsa and Karylle.

201
00:11:06,499 --> 00:11:09,711
I have no idea how they found out.
They even know about SAM closing.

202
00:11:09,794 --> 00:11:10,837
[frustrated sigh]

203
00:11:10,920 --> 00:11:13,131
Maybe Karylle's name

204
00:11:13,214 --> 00:11:15,466
was mentioned on YouTube

205
00:11:15,550 --> 00:11:17,093
or maybe someone's snitching.

206
00:11:17,177 --> 00:11:18,553
I really don't know.

207
00:11:18,636 --> 00:11:19,804
What will you do?

208
00:11:21,139 --> 00:11:24,017
I have to find out who that spy is.

209
00:11:24,475 --> 00:11:26,603
This mess is just getting bigger.

210
00:11:26,686 --> 00:11:30,190
And I will not stop
until I discover who it is.

211
00:11:30,690 --> 00:11:33,151
Okay, I'll gather everything
right now.

212
00:11:44,996 --> 00:11:46,581
[knocking on door]

213
00:11:46,664 --> 00:11:47,665
[Gab] Andrea.

214
00:11:49,667 --> 00:11:51,336
[Andrea] Come in!

215
00:11:54,047 --> 00:11:55,215
I'm here!

216
00:11:58,426 --> 00:11:59,427
Why is it so dark?

217
00:12:08,770 --> 00:12:10,355
- [Andrea clears throat]
- I'm so hungry.

218
00:12:10,813 --> 00:12:11,814
Oh!

219
00:12:11,898 --> 00:12:13,024
Another costume party?

220
00:12:15,485 --> 00:12:17,362
Just trying a few things on.

221
00:12:18,571 --> 00:12:20,281
Come! Sit!

222
00:12:20,657 --> 00:12:21,658
Wait.

223
00:12:22,492 --> 00:12:24,327
I'm really hungry. You hungry?

224
00:12:24,577 --> 00:12:26,204
[Andrea] Come on!

225
00:12:26,287 --> 00:12:27,330
Here I go.

226
00:12:29,123 --> 00:12:30,166
I just remembered.

227
00:12:30,250 --> 00:12:33,253
You said the spy

228
00:12:34,337 --> 00:12:36,673
could be one of us in SAM.

229
00:12:36,756 --> 00:12:38,132
But I think...

230
00:12:39,842 --> 00:12:41,970
that's impossible.

231
00:12:42,053 --> 00:12:43,054
I mean...

232
00:12:46,307 --> 00:12:48,685
Remember when you told me

233
00:12:49,936 --> 00:12:52,855
I don't need anything
or anyone to have a baby?

234
00:12:53,982 --> 00:12:56,401
Right, you can do it on your own.

235
00:12:56,484 --> 00:12:59,320
Apparently, I do.

236
00:12:59,737 --> 00:13:01,155
[moans]

237
00:13:02,532 --> 00:13:04,033
- You do?
- Uh-huh.

238
00:13:05,034 --> 00:13:06,160
What?

239
00:13:06,411 --> 00:13:08,413
[playful music]

240
00:13:10,748 --> 00:13:11,749
How about it?

241
00:13:12,417 --> 00:13:13,501
Why me?

242
00:13:13,584 --> 00:13:14,794
Who else?

243
00:13:14,877 --> 00:13:17,380
- Who else? Come on.
- What do you mean "who else"?

244
00:13:17,463 --> 00:13:18,840
- Come...
- [Gab] Hey!

245
00:13:19,257 --> 00:13:20,633
Stop it. Matthew!

246
00:13:20,717 --> 00:13:22,093
He's made two babies already!

247
00:13:22,176 --> 00:13:23,886
- [Andrea] I know!
- I only have one kid!

248
00:13:23,970 --> 00:13:25,513
No! His is too old,
and it might not work!

249
00:13:25,596 --> 00:13:26,931
- I want you!
- How about male exes?

250
00:13:27,015 --> 00:13:28,349
Come on, please!

251
00:13:28,433 --> 00:13:29,851
No way, I'm going home!

252
00:13:30,310 --> 00:13:31,311
Hey!

253
00:13:31,978 --> 00:13:33,104
I'm going home.

254
00:13:34,105 --> 00:13:35,231
Hey!

255
00:13:35,315 --> 00:13:36,733
- Sit. Stay!
- I am not sitting!

256
00:13:36,816 --> 00:13:39,777
I need just that!
You're being selfish!

257
00:13:39,861 --> 00:13:41,487
- You've given away a lot...
- The heck?

258
00:13:41,571 --> 00:13:43,323
...but you won't give me some?

259
00:13:43,406 --> 00:13:44,407
Are you drunk?

260
00:13:44,490 --> 00:13:46,117
- Come on!
- [Gab] No way!

261
00:13:46,200 --> 00:13:47,869
[Andrea] It'll just be quick, right?

262
00:13:47,952 --> 00:13:49,203
Let's do it!

263
00:13:49,287 --> 00:13:50,538
- Help!
- Just close your eyes.

264
00:13:50,621 --> 00:13:52,707
I'm still a woman! Don't be choosy!

265
00:13:52,790 --> 00:13:54,208
I swear I'm gonna hit you!

266
00:13:54,292 --> 00:13:55,710
- Please!
- I said I wanna go home!

267
00:13:55,793 --> 00:13:57,503
- Let's get this over with!
- [loud thud]

268
00:13:59,255 --> 00:14:00,340
[Gab] Ouch! That hurts!

269
00:14:00,423 --> 00:14:01,758
[Andrea] Selfish jerk.

270
00:14:01,841 --> 00:14:02,925
Fine, keep your sperm!

271
00:14:03,843 --> 00:14:07,764
- [Gab] Is this blood? Is it mine?
- [Andrea laughs]

272
00:14:08,848 --> 00:14:10,683
I changed my mind.

273
00:14:10,767 --> 00:14:12,185
This is too tough. Some other time.

274
00:14:13,311 --> 00:14:15,146
You've slept with men before, right?

275
00:14:15,855 --> 00:14:18,775
Yeah, but I didn't enjoy myself.

276
00:14:18,858 --> 00:14:21,527
Just like I didn't enjoy
having to seduce you.

277
00:14:21,861 --> 00:14:24,781
Hey, no means no, even for me.

278
00:14:24,864 --> 00:14:27,116
You pushed.
And now you're insulting me.

279
00:14:28,284 --> 00:14:29,285
[chuckles]

280
00:14:29,369 --> 00:14:30,620
Can I tell Matthew?

281
00:14:30,703 --> 00:14:32,705
- Please no.
- Come on!

282
00:14:32,789 --> 00:14:33,790
He needs a good laugh!

283
00:14:34,457 --> 00:14:36,042
Wow. You mean he's still depressed?

284
00:14:36,125 --> 00:14:37,877
Yes. He's really down.

285
00:14:38,419 --> 00:14:40,129
And you'll use me for a laugh?

286
00:14:40,380 --> 00:14:42,590
No sense in letting
that costume go to waste.

287
00:14:44,342 --> 00:14:46,636
It's cute, though.

288
00:14:47,220 --> 00:14:48,471
But you know...

289
00:14:49,263 --> 00:14:51,599
there are things in my life
that I can't lose.

290
00:14:52,308 --> 00:14:53,851
I wouldn't survive without them.

291
00:14:55,228 --> 00:14:57,021
[Andrea] There's my mom, of course.

292
00:14:57,105 --> 00:14:58,189
Top of the list.

293
00:14:59,065 --> 00:15:02,610
Well, of course, granted
she's not really there anymore.

294
00:15:02,693 --> 00:15:04,529
But you know, she's just there.

295
00:15:06,030 --> 00:15:07,949
I'll still take what I can get.

296
00:15:09,409 --> 00:15:10,952
And of course I can't lose you.

297
00:15:12,412 --> 00:15:14,539
Like I can't lose SAM.

298
00:15:16,165 --> 00:15:17,333
So this baby thing...

299
00:15:18,376 --> 00:15:19,627
I'll have to park it for now.

300
00:15:19,710 --> 00:15:21,546
There's just too much

301
00:15:22,338 --> 00:15:23,631
we need to do for SAM.

302
00:15:24,757 --> 00:15:26,092
- I'll get to it one day.
- Okay.

303
00:15:26,676 --> 00:15:29,679
Okay. Can you put on a jacket now?

304
00:15:31,180 --> 00:15:32,432
You believe him?

305
00:15:32,515 --> 00:15:33,641
[Brandon over phone] I told you.

306
00:15:34,308 --> 00:15:36,644
[in English] I don't want to pay
for any breach of contract.

307
00:15:38,438 --> 00:15:40,273
If Galaxy can talk to our brands

308
00:15:40,857 --> 00:15:42,358
and fix this mess

309
00:15:42,650 --> 00:15:44,318
why should I not let them?

310
00:15:44,402 --> 00:15:46,195
[in Filipino] Brandon,
you still have a few more months

311
00:15:46,279 --> 00:15:47,655
on your SAM contract.

312
00:15:47,738 --> 00:15:48,906
I know.

313
00:15:49,574 --> 00:15:51,117
[in English]
That's why I'm telling you now.

314
00:15:51,451 --> 00:15:53,327
- [dial tone beeping]
- [clears throat]

315
00:15:58,749 --> 00:15:59,959
[in Filipino] What do we have today?

316
00:16:00,042 --> 00:16:04,130
[in English] That's a list
of our Social Media Division clients

317
00:16:04,213 --> 00:16:08,176
their current endorsements,
and other obligations.

318
00:16:10,470 --> 00:16:11,888
[Matthew in Filipino]
What am I looking at?

319
00:16:12,597 --> 00:16:14,474
I can never understand those numbers.

320
00:16:15,808 --> 00:16:18,686
[Noemi] These are just comparatives
to avoid conflict of interest.

321
00:16:21,230 --> 00:16:23,441
[in English]
Speaking of conflict of interest.

322
00:16:33,326 --> 00:16:34,660
Where did you get that?

323
00:16:34,744 --> 00:16:36,204
[in Filipino]
Is this your solution, Matthew?

324
00:16:37,997 --> 00:16:39,957
This is what you meant
when you said "I'll take care of it?"

325
00:16:41,959 --> 00:16:43,461
Well, if you're leaving us

326
00:16:43,836 --> 00:16:47,006
now tell me, how the heck
are we gonna buy SAM?

327
00:16:47,089 --> 00:16:49,342
Calm down, Andrea.
I haven't signed anything yet.

328
00:16:49,425 --> 00:16:51,052
- [Andrea] Yet?
- He hasn't decided!

329
00:16:51,761 --> 00:16:53,346
And you knew about this?

330
00:16:55,097 --> 00:16:56,807
You didn't even bother telling me?

331
00:16:57,266 --> 00:17:01,062
And you dared to look me in the eye
and tell me I could trust you.

332
00:17:01,145 --> 00:17:02,271
How dare you!

333
00:17:02,855 --> 00:17:04,982
Wait! What is happening?

334
00:17:05,274 --> 00:17:07,068
Matthew? You're moving?

335
00:17:07,568 --> 00:17:08,611
To Galaxy?

336
00:17:10,738 --> 00:17:12,698
Not before I fix our problems.

337
00:17:13,366 --> 00:17:14,700
Give me that! This one.

338
00:17:15,076 --> 00:17:16,285
Give it to me!

339
00:17:17,203 --> 00:17:19,330
This is our biggest problem.

340
00:17:20,373 --> 00:17:21,374
This!

341
00:17:24,210 --> 00:17:26,212
Guys, can you step outside?

342
00:17:26,295 --> 00:17:28,548
No! Let them freaking stay.

343
00:17:30,049 --> 00:17:32,218
[Andrea] Let them know
and hear us say it.

344
00:17:32,301 --> 00:17:34,011
That there will be no junior manager

345
00:17:34,637 --> 00:17:36,514
no more Social Media Division

346
00:17:36,597 --> 00:17:37,848
and no more artists to manage

347
00:17:37,932 --> 00:17:39,559
because there will be no more SAM!

348
00:17:40,142 --> 00:17:43,145
[dramatic music]

349
00:17:51,195 --> 00:17:52,196
Chin.

350
00:17:54,991 --> 00:17:57,076
- Chin! What did you just do?
- What do you mean what did I do?

351
00:17:57,159 --> 00:17:59,620
You and I are the only ones
who saw that contract.

352
00:18:00,079 --> 00:18:01,872
You told me not to tell Ms. Andrea!

353
00:18:02,498 --> 00:18:04,750
- You told me not to get involved.
- Because they are going to fight.

354
00:18:04,834 --> 00:18:06,002
And I was right!

355
00:18:06,460 --> 00:18:09,672
[Chin] Why does it sound like
you're accusing me?

356
00:18:10,923 --> 00:18:13,467
You were holding
your father's contract.

357
00:18:14,218 --> 00:18:16,053
You're the one who left it.

358
00:18:16,387 --> 00:18:18,097
Why are you blaming me?

359
00:18:27,857 --> 00:18:30,693
This is not the business
for friendship.

360
00:18:32,278 --> 00:18:34,780
This isn't college or high school.

361
00:18:36,282 --> 00:18:40,036
It's the toughest place
to find someone to trust.

362
00:18:41,245 --> 00:18:43,122
I've been in this business
for a long time.

363
00:18:43,914 --> 00:18:45,374
I've met so many people.

364
00:18:46,167 --> 00:18:47,209
But friends?

365
00:18:48,294 --> 00:18:49,629
I could count them on one hand.

366
00:18:51,088 --> 00:18:53,591
Real friends are hard to find here.

367
00:18:56,510 --> 00:18:57,803
[in English] It's not what you think.

368
00:19:01,349 --> 00:19:03,392
I've been trying to hold off
making this decision

369
00:19:03,476 --> 00:19:04,518
for as long as I could.

370
00:19:04,852 --> 00:19:06,354
You should have told us.

371
00:19:08,022 --> 00:19:10,441
[in Filipino] There's no way
we can buy SAM on our own.

372
00:19:13,861 --> 00:19:15,321
Let's not talk about this now.

373
00:19:15,946 --> 00:19:17,490
[in English]
We have to talk to Helen first.

374
00:19:19,950 --> 00:19:21,410
What are you planning to tell her?

375
00:19:23,829 --> 00:19:25,748
[in Filipino]
That she can sell SAM to someone else

376
00:19:25,831 --> 00:19:28,042
because we don't have
the money to pay for it?

377
00:19:29,085 --> 00:19:30,378
[in English]
Is that what you're saying?

378
00:19:32,088 --> 00:19:33,214
You just have to trust me.

379
00:19:33,297 --> 00:19:35,716
You're making it very difficult
to trust you.

380
00:19:36,634 --> 00:19:39,470
You lied about Paul,
you lied about Gina

381
00:19:39,553 --> 00:19:41,305
you lied about living here.

382
00:19:41,764 --> 00:19:42,765
About Camille!

383
00:19:44,433 --> 00:19:45,768
And who knows what else?

384
00:19:47,687 --> 00:19:48,688
You know...

385
00:19:52,733 --> 00:19:54,360
it may not seem like it now...

386
00:19:58,030 --> 00:19:59,240
but I'm doing this for you.

387
00:20:00,533 --> 00:20:02,493
- I'm doing this for Samuel.
- Oh, no.

388
00:20:02,868 --> 00:20:04,036
Don't you dare...

389
00:20:04,954 --> 00:20:07,707
Don't you dare say that.

390
00:20:07,915 --> 00:20:09,709
[mouths] Don't you dare.

391
00:20:10,543 --> 00:20:12,002
- [Gab] Hold on.
- [Andrea] Don't you dare.

392
00:20:12,837 --> 00:20:15,131
[cell phone ringing]

393
00:20:15,506 --> 00:20:16,966
- [Gab] What do you even...
- Wait.

394
00:20:20,219 --> 00:20:21,220
It's Helen.

395
00:20:26,225 --> 00:20:28,227
No one comes to see me.

396
00:20:31,522 --> 00:20:33,441
I don't pull up ratings anymore.

397
00:20:33,816 --> 00:20:35,901
WE LOVE YOU

398
00:20:35,985 --> 00:20:37,069
But...

399
00:20:37,528 --> 00:20:38,529
But!

400
00:20:38,612 --> 00:20:39,989
KEEP FIGHTING!

401
00:20:41,907 --> 00:20:43,325
- I want to thank...
- [notification pings]

402
00:20:44,577 --> 00:20:47,538
...each and every one of you

403
00:20:47,621 --> 00:20:50,458
for all those years.

404
00:20:50,541 --> 00:20:53,377
All the love and support

405
00:20:53,461 --> 00:20:56,255
that you've given me all these years.

406
00:20:56,338 --> 00:20:57,840
Thank you very much.

407
00:20:57,923 --> 00:20:59,967
- Ms. Karylle?
- Yeah?

408
00:21:00,050 --> 00:21:03,679
- ...but I just have one request.
- Ms. Eula, excuse me. Thank you.

409
00:21:03,763 --> 00:21:05,890
- Look.
- Is that Mama?

410
00:21:05,973 --> 00:21:08,726
- For all the years you have given me
- Is it live?

411
00:21:08,809 --> 00:21:11,812
all that love and support...

412
00:21:13,355 --> 00:21:14,732
Please give it

413
00:21:15,191 --> 00:21:17,318
wholeheartedly to Karylle.

414
00:21:19,487 --> 00:21:20,529
Helen.

415
00:21:21,822 --> 00:21:23,491
[in English]
We just want to know where we stand.

416
00:21:26,577 --> 00:21:27,578
Helen.

417
00:21:28,662 --> 00:21:30,623
Please don't sell SAM to Paul Amir.

418
00:21:32,333 --> 00:21:34,084
Galaxy doesn't deserve SAM.

419
00:21:34,418 --> 00:21:35,461
[in Filipino] Samuel...

420
00:21:35,961 --> 00:21:38,881
would claw his way out of the grave
if he knew this would happen.

421
00:21:39,924 --> 00:21:41,717
What has this got to do with Samuel?

422
00:21:43,469 --> 00:21:47,389
He would never sell SAM
if he were alive.

423
00:21:48,682 --> 00:21:50,017
But he's dead.

424
00:21:51,519 --> 00:21:55,397
I'm surprised you weren't aware
that Galaxy is out of the picture.

425
00:22:01,904 --> 00:22:05,491
[in English]
You were this close to losing SAM.

426
00:22:11,121 --> 00:22:12,790
[Helen] And I'm selling SAM...

427
00:22:14,124 --> 00:22:15,125
to you.

428
00:22:18,295 --> 00:22:19,296
Oh...

429
00:22:21,257 --> 00:22:23,717
[in Filipino] I was going to call you
tomorrow anyway

430
00:22:23,801 --> 00:22:25,553
to discuss the documents.

431
00:22:26,053 --> 00:22:27,555
[in English]
Whatever has to be signed.

432
00:22:30,015 --> 00:22:31,684
And the check, of course.

433
00:22:32,977 --> 00:22:35,271
[Helen] I'll give you one week

434
00:22:35,354 --> 00:22:36,814
to pull the money.

435
00:22:41,110 --> 00:22:42,152
[in Filipino] So...

436
00:22:43,195 --> 00:22:46,323
you told Paul
you were moving to Galaxy...

437
00:22:48,200 --> 00:22:49,785
Thank you so much.

438
00:22:51,287 --> 00:22:54,373
[Gab] ...if he withdrew his offer
to Helen.

439
00:22:55,791 --> 00:22:57,001
He would have stopped at nothing

440
00:22:57,668 --> 00:22:59,712
until Galaxy was number one.

441
00:23:00,296 --> 00:23:02,172
I hate you, Matthew.

442
00:23:02,798 --> 00:23:04,008
Darn you.

443
00:23:05,050 --> 00:23:07,011
[in English]
He's really bent on taking us down.

444
00:23:08,721 --> 00:23:09,722
Matt.

445
00:23:10,681 --> 00:23:11,682
Thank you.

446
00:23:15,227 --> 00:23:16,478
Don't touch me, Andrea.

447
00:23:20,107 --> 00:23:21,275
You really hurt me.

448
00:23:21,358 --> 00:23:23,777
I know.

449
00:23:24,278 --> 00:23:26,071
[in Filipino] But you know me.

450
00:23:26,572 --> 00:23:29,158
I'm sorry you got caught in my anger.

451
00:23:29,742 --> 00:23:30,868
I'm sorry.

452
00:23:31,410 --> 00:23:32,411
Please.

453
00:23:34,872 --> 00:23:37,583
- [laughs]
- What?

454
00:23:38,334 --> 00:23:39,793
I'm not angry.

455
00:23:40,419 --> 00:23:42,504
I just wanted to see you
beg me for forgiveness.

456
00:23:42,588 --> 00:23:43,797
I hate you!

457
00:23:43,881 --> 00:23:46,050
[all laugh]

458
00:23:47,301 --> 00:23:48,344
So we're good?

459
00:23:48,427 --> 00:23:49,845
- We sure are.
- Yay!

460
00:23:49,929 --> 00:23:50,930
We sure are.

461
00:23:53,849 --> 00:23:57,144
- You're so annoying.
- [Gab laughing sarcastically]

462
00:23:57,227 --> 00:23:59,939
- Aren't you?
- It's not that funny.

463
00:24:00,022 --> 00:24:01,148
Where do we get the money?

464
00:24:01,607 --> 00:24:02,650
You know...

465
00:24:02,733 --> 00:24:04,693
Gabriel, use your head, will you?

466
00:24:04,777 --> 00:24:05,986
[scoffs] Wow.

467
00:24:06,070 --> 00:24:09,239
No one else is buying SAM except us.

468
00:24:09,323 --> 00:24:10,366
- Mm-hm.
- I mean...

469
00:24:10,449 --> 00:24:12,493
Helen was wrong, you know.

470
00:24:12,576 --> 00:24:15,955
No one else would want SAM
more than us.

471
00:24:16,413 --> 00:24:17,414
I agree.

472
00:24:17,498 --> 00:24:20,542
So whatever happens, happens.

473
00:24:21,168 --> 00:24:24,213
The only concern now
is the money, but...

474
00:24:24,296 --> 00:24:25,297
That's a piece of cake.

475
00:24:25,381 --> 00:24:26,715
Whatever will be, will be.

476
00:24:26,799 --> 00:24:29,176
[upbeat music]

477
00:24:48,696 --> 00:24:49,738
[in English] Hello, everyone!

478
00:24:49,822 --> 00:24:51,991
Good morning! Where are my boys?

479
00:24:52,992 --> 00:24:55,077
- [in Filipino] Upstairs.
- Good!

480
00:24:55,160 --> 00:24:58,205
Deo, what's happening to your face?
Are you having a stroke?

481
00:24:58,831 --> 00:25:01,250
Let that flow! Rainfall is lucky!

482
00:25:02,292 --> 00:25:05,212
[in English] Good morning, boys!

483
00:25:05,504 --> 00:25:07,006
- How are my boys today?
- [Gab] Good morning.

484
00:25:07,089 --> 00:25:09,341
- Good morning, thank you very much!
- Coffee all around!

485
00:25:09,633 --> 00:25:11,135
- Wow!
- Are you guys ready to work?

486
00:25:11,218 --> 00:25:12,219
[Andrea] Let's get to work!

487
00:25:12,302 --> 00:25:14,722
- Oh, I'm so happy!
- No more coffee for you.

488
00:25:14,805 --> 00:25:17,224
You might pull
your bunny act on Gabriel again.

489
00:25:17,307 --> 00:25:18,767
Don't worry, you're next!

490
00:25:18,851 --> 00:25:20,853
- [chuckles]
- Anyway...

491
00:25:22,271 --> 00:25:23,939
Are you guys ready to work today?

492
00:25:24,398 --> 00:25:26,859
I feel so positive today.

493
00:25:26,942 --> 00:25:29,028
I'm pitching
our social media strategy

494
00:25:29,111 --> 00:25:31,030
to my new talents.

495
00:25:31,655 --> 00:25:33,949
So where's the energy here?

496
00:25:35,617 --> 00:25:37,953
[thrilling music]

497
00:25:38,037 --> 00:25:39,663
Yeah, Sofie mentioned it.

498
00:25:39,747 --> 00:25:41,290
We'll take care of you, Lao.

499
00:25:42,249 --> 00:25:43,250
Influencers!

500
00:25:44,334 --> 00:25:47,004
We haven't forgotten
what you did for Laurice.

501
00:25:47,087 --> 00:25:48,088
[Andrea] Yes, Elisse.

502
00:25:48,172 --> 00:25:49,923
- We got you.
- It's perfect for you.

503
00:25:50,007 --> 00:25:52,426
Lav's been working on this for years.

504
00:25:53,260 --> 00:25:55,179
Hey, Andrea! Influencers!

505
00:25:55,721 --> 00:25:56,764
Yes.

506
00:25:57,306 --> 00:26:00,059
Sir Gab, did you like it?

507
00:26:00,142 --> 00:26:01,560
Hi, Janine!

508
00:26:01,894 --> 00:26:02,978
Yeah!

509
00:26:03,062 --> 00:26:04,730
Well, about your renewal contract.

510
00:26:04,813 --> 00:26:06,690
What's going on?
You never got back to me.

511
00:26:08,567 --> 00:26:09,818
Is that from HBO?

512
00:26:10,527 --> 00:26:11,653
Um...

513
00:26:11,737 --> 00:26:12,821
We're working on it!

514
00:26:12,905 --> 00:26:14,114
Um...

515
00:26:14,198 --> 00:26:15,991
Just working out
the schedules with them.

516
00:26:16,658 --> 00:26:17,910
So the project is still a go?

517
00:26:18,327 --> 00:26:19,411
I heard about Rob.

518
00:26:19,495 --> 00:26:22,081
Of course, it's a go!

519
00:26:22,164 --> 00:26:24,041
Actually, we're done with casting.

520
00:26:24,124 --> 00:26:25,250
[scoffs]

521
00:26:26,085 --> 00:26:29,171
Call me when you have
the HBO contract for me to sign.

522
00:26:29,588 --> 00:26:31,757
[in English]
Until then, I'm a free agent, okay?

523
00:26:31,840 --> 00:26:34,259
- [Janine over phone] Bye, Andrea!
- Wait!

524
00:26:34,343 --> 00:26:35,803
[Andrea over phone]
Hear me out first, okay?

525
00:26:37,179 --> 00:26:38,680
Something's in the works here at SAM.

526
00:26:38,764 --> 00:26:41,058
And we're building
social media content

527
00:26:41,141 --> 00:26:42,184
for our artists.

528
00:26:42,267 --> 00:26:44,937
And I think this is
a very good platform for you.

529
00:26:45,312 --> 00:26:46,313
Um...

530
00:26:46,855 --> 00:26:50,359
I can see you getting brands,
more brands!

531
00:26:50,442 --> 00:26:51,652
A lot of endorsements!

532
00:26:51,735 --> 00:26:56,031
- See?
- Wait, did you say social media?

533
00:26:56,115 --> 00:26:59,451
Yes, social media
is the way to go, apparently.

534
00:26:59,535 --> 00:27:02,037
You know, times are changing...

535
00:27:02,121 --> 00:27:03,205
True!

536
00:27:03,288 --> 00:27:06,834
Like weren't we just talking about
a lead role in a Hollywood film?

537
00:27:07,501 --> 00:27:09,795
Times really are changing,
right, Andrea?

538
00:27:11,630 --> 00:27:12,840
[grumbles]

539
00:27:16,552 --> 00:27:19,513
- Good night, Ms. Andrea.
- [Andrea] This still isn't fixed?

540
00:27:20,097 --> 00:27:22,724
That's crazy. Get it done!

541
00:27:23,684 --> 00:27:24,685
- [Gab] Andrea.
- What?

542
00:27:24,768 --> 00:27:26,603
Let's go. Drinks.
We need to unwind. Relax.

543
00:27:26,687 --> 00:27:30,232
Yeah, a drink before bedtime
would be great.

544
00:27:30,315 --> 00:27:32,067
So I won't have to listen
to him snore.

545
00:27:32,151 --> 00:27:33,360
Maybe I'll fall asleep a lot sooner.

546
00:27:33,443 --> 00:27:34,778
- Oh, really.
- No, I'm going home.

547
00:27:34,862 --> 00:27:36,113
- Just a drink!
- We won't be long!

548
00:27:36,196 --> 00:27:38,115
I said no! I want to go home.

549
00:27:38,198 --> 00:27:39,199
You go.

550
00:27:39,741 --> 00:27:41,827
That's an ugly jacket, burn it.

551
00:27:47,249 --> 00:27:48,333
[in English] She's back.

552
00:27:49,418 --> 00:27:50,961
It was fun while it lasted.

553
00:27:54,631 --> 00:27:57,509
[in Filipino] Whoever they are,
the source of the leaks

554
00:27:57,968 --> 00:27:59,344
they're really good.

555
00:28:03,849 --> 00:28:05,184
What are you doing?

556
00:28:05,767 --> 00:28:10,439
Taking a snapshot
so I can find it quicker.

557
00:28:14,026 --> 00:28:15,027
[gasps]

558
00:28:16,945 --> 00:28:18,405
Here we go!

559
00:28:23,535 --> 00:28:24,578
What's that?

560
00:28:25,287 --> 00:28:26,413
[Sofie] A charm!

561
00:28:27,247 --> 00:28:28,999
[squeals, giggles]

562
00:28:30,459 --> 00:28:31,501
I like it!

563
00:28:34,129 --> 00:28:35,672
Pretty!

564
00:28:36,798 --> 00:28:37,841
Looks good, huh?

565
00:28:40,802 --> 00:28:42,804
[inquisitive music]

566
00:28:49,478 --> 00:28:50,604
[Andrea] If Maricel
and Snooky leave...

567
00:28:50,687 --> 00:28:51,813
[Ogie] ...wanted to take over SAM.

568
00:28:51,897 --> 00:28:53,565
- [Gab] Frank Villacin!
- [Ogie] Karylle, Zsa Zsa.

569
00:28:53,649 --> 00:28:55,525
- [Mr. Fu] Rob Gomez.
- [Ogie] Lav Diaz and Monsour.

570
00:28:55,609 --> 00:28:58,779
[Mr. Fu] What did Rob do
to deserve this?

571
00:29:05,494 --> 00:29:07,829
[line ringing]

572
00:29:07,913 --> 00:29:08,914
Hello?

573
00:29:08,997 --> 00:29:09,998
Uh...

574
00:29:12,209 --> 00:29:15,087
I know where the leaks are from.

575
00:29:22,010 --> 00:29:23,679
Why is Daisy here?

576
00:29:24,054 --> 00:29:26,598
[gasps] That's okay, I'm not busy.

577
00:29:27,349 --> 00:29:29,893
How about a snack? I brought palabok.

578
00:29:30,811 --> 00:29:33,480
Noemi, what is this?

579
00:29:33,563 --> 00:29:35,023
Do you not have a life?

580
00:29:37,192 --> 00:29:38,193
[Daisy] Have a snack.

581
00:29:39,695 --> 00:29:40,988
Um...

582
00:29:41,071 --> 00:29:42,531
We have to talk.

583
00:29:43,198 --> 00:29:44,950
Is this some kind of intervention?

584
00:29:45,659 --> 00:29:46,660
Sort of.

585
00:29:47,452 --> 00:29:48,704
We're not friends enough for that.

586
00:29:54,710 --> 00:29:55,711
It was you!

587
00:29:56,586 --> 00:30:00,090
You leaked all those rumors
about SAM!

588
00:30:00,173 --> 00:30:01,216
[shrieks]

589
00:30:01,300 --> 00:30:02,301
You?

590
00:30:02,718 --> 00:30:03,760
You did that?

591
00:30:04,094 --> 00:30:05,304
- [Sofie] Noemi.
- [Daisy] Oh, gosh.

592
00:30:05,387 --> 00:30:06,722
- [knocks on door]
- Don't even try...

593
00:30:07,180 --> 00:30:09,391
Camille, we're all sleeping here.

594
00:30:09,474 --> 00:30:10,642
Sorry, Valerie.

595
00:30:11,310 --> 00:30:12,477
[Chin] We're sorry.

596
00:30:12,561 --> 00:30:13,854
- Daisy, shut up.
- Shut the door.

597
00:30:13,937 --> 00:30:15,314
[Sofie] You're too loud.

598
00:30:15,397 --> 00:30:17,441
No way, it was you?

599
00:30:18,400 --> 00:30:20,110
Really, sis?

600
00:30:22,904 --> 00:30:25,115
- What are you talking about?
- [Noemi] Don't deny it, Chin.

601
00:30:25,657 --> 00:30:29,077
That picture
of Maricel and Snooky fighting?

602
00:30:30,829 --> 00:30:32,414
You were on the set that day.

603
00:30:33,790 --> 00:30:35,917
And so was Camille.

604
00:30:36,293 --> 00:30:38,545
But they were not fighting
when I was there.

605
00:30:39,379 --> 00:30:41,673
You know about Zsa Zsa and Karylle

606
00:30:41,757 --> 00:30:43,091
and Brandon's issues too.

607
00:30:43,175 --> 00:30:44,593
And even about SAM closing.

608
00:30:45,218 --> 00:30:46,887
You all know about that!

609
00:30:47,596 --> 00:30:49,598
That bedazzled phone is yours!

610
00:30:49,681 --> 00:30:53,226
[Noemi] We saw its reflection
in Rob's picture at the hospital.

611
00:30:59,816 --> 00:31:00,901
Okay.

612
00:31:03,028 --> 00:31:04,279
So what are you going to do?

613
00:31:04,946 --> 00:31:08,492
Are you going to gang up on me
and beat me up? Come on.

614
00:31:08,867 --> 00:31:10,827
- [Chin] Come on.
- Don't be overdramatic.

615
00:31:14,748 --> 00:31:16,166
How could you do that, Chin?

616
00:31:17,167 --> 00:31:19,711
- I don't owe you any explanation...
- [Camille] I meant to Rob.

617
00:31:23,215 --> 00:31:24,716
How could you do that to Rob?

618
00:31:24,800 --> 00:31:26,593
I'm not doing anything wrong to Rob.

619
00:31:26,676 --> 00:31:28,428
I didn't do anything to him.

620
00:31:30,972 --> 00:31:33,975
I just wanted everyone to know
what Frank Villacin did to him.

621
00:31:34,601 --> 00:31:38,271
Because none of you cared enough
to do that for him.

622
00:31:38,355 --> 00:31:39,773
And what about the other leaks?

623
00:31:44,111 --> 00:31:45,612
I wanted a promotion.

624
00:31:46,696 --> 00:31:48,990
[Sofie] You think
that will get you promoted?

625
00:31:50,575 --> 00:31:51,743
Not in SAM.

626
00:31:55,914 --> 00:31:56,957
You're leaving?

627
00:31:59,960 --> 00:32:01,002
Noemi...

628
00:32:02,337 --> 00:32:04,131
you've been with SAM for so long.

629
00:32:04,381 --> 00:32:07,509
[Chin] You can do your job
with your eyes closed!

630
00:32:08,343 --> 00:32:11,805
If Matthew calls in sick,
you can easily do his work for him.

631
00:32:13,807 --> 00:32:17,352
I can't compete
with the boss's child.

632
00:32:17,436 --> 00:32:18,645
That has nothing to do with work!

633
00:32:18,728 --> 00:32:20,021
Says the nepo baby!

634
00:32:20,105 --> 00:32:21,565
Nepo baby?

635
00:32:22,566 --> 00:32:24,025
No matter what I do...

636
00:32:25,068 --> 00:32:26,570
I'm overlooked and underappreciated.

637
00:32:28,155 --> 00:32:30,031
What are you talking about?

638
00:32:30,115 --> 00:32:31,283
That's not true.

639
00:32:31,366 --> 00:32:34,744
Sir Gab always tells me
he can't do any of this without you.

640
00:32:34,828 --> 00:32:36,580
[Sofie] You should have
talked to him first.

641
00:32:36,663 --> 00:32:37,956
Or us!

642
00:32:39,374 --> 00:32:41,751
Chin, we're in this together!

643
00:32:43,712 --> 00:32:45,839
[Noemi] We started nearly
at the same time.

644
00:32:45,922 --> 00:32:48,133
We panicked and were stupid together.

645
00:32:48,800 --> 00:32:51,136
We were both new, don't you remember?

646
00:32:52,220 --> 00:32:54,055
And now you're leaving like this.

647
00:32:58,101 --> 00:32:59,436
You're with SAM, Chin.

648
00:33:01,396 --> 00:33:03,523
If you want this promotion so bad

649
00:33:04,024 --> 00:33:06,109
you can have
the junior manager position!

650
00:33:06,193 --> 00:33:07,402
Oh, please.

651
00:33:07,736 --> 00:33:09,821
I don't care for handouts.

652
00:33:10,614 --> 00:33:14,075
I'll leave you two
to wrestle for it, because...

653
00:33:14,784 --> 00:33:16,995
I'll be a manager at Galaxy.

654
00:33:17,287 --> 00:33:18,288
[Daisy] What?

655
00:33:18,371 --> 00:33:20,332
- Are you ready to be a manager?
- Daisy!

656
00:33:21,416 --> 00:33:22,417
Uh...

657
00:33:22,959 --> 00:33:26,213
I just meant it's a difficult job!

658
00:33:26,296 --> 00:33:28,381
It's tough work to be a manager.

659
00:33:28,465 --> 00:33:30,133
Maybe I don't care.

660
00:33:31,593 --> 00:33:34,846
I know for sure
you're all telling on me.

661
00:33:36,306 --> 00:33:39,559
No worries.
I'll speak to Sir Gab tomorrow.

662
00:33:39,643 --> 00:33:41,978
You won't see me again after that.

663
00:33:47,859 --> 00:33:48,902
Chin!

664
00:33:48,985 --> 00:33:50,195
I'm leaving.

665
00:33:51,488 --> 00:33:53,240
- I'll borrow some cash for my fare.
- [Noemi] But...

666
00:33:54,032 --> 00:33:56,117
That's my cab fare, Chin!

667
00:33:57,077 --> 00:33:59,162
[Daisy] What's up with Chin?

668
00:33:59,829 --> 00:34:01,373
What will Sir Gab say

669
00:34:01,456 --> 00:34:03,667
when he finds out
this is all Chin's doing?

670
00:34:06,086 --> 00:34:07,337
[knocks on door]

671
00:34:07,754 --> 00:34:10,090
- [Karylle] Mama?
- [knocking continues]

672
00:34:10,173 --> 00:34:11,299
It's open.

673
00:34:13,677 --> 00:34:14,761
[relieved sigh]

674
00:34:14,844 --> 00:34:17,055
You didn't tell me you were coming.

675
00:34:19,724 --> 00:34:20,809
Mama.

676
00:34:21,142 --> 00:34:23,103
What are you doing to yourself?

677
00:34:23,186 --> 00:34:25,063
I don't know, K.

678
00:34:26,898 --> 00:34:29,776
I just feel so alone.

679
00:34:33,822 --> 00:34:34,906
[sobs]

680
00:34:34,990 --> 00:34:36,491
I worked so hard

681
00:34:36,825 --> 00:34:39,286
to give you everything.

682
00:34:41,371 --> 00:34:43,331
But it seems I've given you nothing.

683
00:34:46,001 --> 00:34:47,002
Mom.

684
00:34:47,669 --> 00:34:48,920
Listen to me.

685
00:34:49,504 --> 00:34:50,880
I'm not your fan.

686
00:34:52,257 --> 00:34:53,258
I get it.

687
00:34:54,718 --> 00:34:55,719
No, you don't.

688
00:34:56,553 --> 00:34:59,848
I'm not a fan who disappears on you

689
00:35:00,181 --> 00:35:01,725
when she finds someone new to stan.

690
00:35:01,808 --> 00:35:05,437
I'm not a fan who's here today
but gone tomorrow.

691
00:35:08,273 --> 00:35:09,482
I'm your daughter.

692
00:35:11,359 --> 00:35:13,403
I will always be your daughter.

693
00:35:14,946 --> 00:35:16,781
I am not the enemy.

694
00:35:21,286 --> 00:35:23,705
But I'm not you either.

695
00:35:24,914 --> 00:35:26,291
When I sing, I don't need

696
00:35:26,374 --> 00:35:29,169
everyone else in the stadium

697
00:35:29,252 --> 00:35:30,837
to sing along with me.

698
00:35:32,297 --> 00:35:33,673
If I write a song

699
00:35:34,090 --> 00:35:37,969
I don't need the album
to go triple platinum or something.

700
00:35:39,095 --> 00:35:43,391
But in everything that I do...

701
00:35:44,934 --> 00:35:46,061
know that

702
00:35:47,729 --> 00:35:49,439
I want to make you proud.

703
00:35:49,981 --> 00:35:51,983
[somber music]

704
00:35:56,071 --> 00:35:58,073
[sobs]

705
00:35:58,865 --> 00:36:00,325
Can you forgive me?

706
00:36:04,412 --> 00:36:05,622
[chuckles]

707
00:36:10,168 --> 00:36:11,878
[clacking]

708
00:36:30,855 --> 00:36:32,107
Why are you here?

709
00:36:34,609 --> 00:36:36,444
Deo's fixing a leak
near Sofie's desk.

710
00:36:37,529 --> 00:36:39,280
It's too noisy for me there.

711
00:36:40,532 --> 00:36:41,616
Chin...

712
00:36:42,909 --> 00:36:44,035
You're wrong about me.

713
00:36:45,620 --> 00:36:47,372
You're wrong about Sir Matthew.

714
00:36:47,455 --> 00:36:48,707
And Ms. Andrea.

715
00:36:50,375 --> 00:36:51,376
And Sir Gab.

716
00:36:51,668 --> 00:36:52,669
You know them well.

717
00:36:53,920 --> 00:36:56,297
Our chances for junior manager
are even, Chin.

718
00:37:18,069 --> 00:37:19,404
Chin, I'm sorry.

719
00:37:22,407 --> 00:37:25,785
It's my fault that you don't like me.

720
00:37:28,538 --> 00:37:30,373
I didn't tell you

721
00:37:30,915 --> 00:37:32,459
that Sir Matthew is my dad.

722
00:37:34,669 --> 00:37:37,213
Our relationship started with a lie.

723
00:37:40,800 --> 00:37:42,802
Maybe if I told you when we first met

724
00:37:43,344 --> 00:37:45,054
it would be easier to trust me.

725
00:37:45,138 --> 00:37:46,139
But really...

726
00:37:47,098 --> 00:37:50,435
it was me who didn't trust you guys.

727
00:37:50,518 --> 00:37:51,895
I didn't think you'd understand

728
00:37:54,105 --> 00:37:56,733
that I really wanted
to work here at SAM

729
00:37:58,443 --> 00:38:00,528
and be with Sir Matthew.

730
00:38:04,449 --> 00:38:05,867
I love SAM, Chin.

731
00:38:09,913 --> 00:38:11,623
That's why I'm doing my best.

732
00:38:12,624 --> 00:38:14,292
I'm not here to compete with you.

733
00:38:20,340 --> 00:38:21,674
Don't leave.

734
00:38:24,427 --> 00:38:27,889
If you really can't stand me,
then I'll leave.

735
00:38:37,148 --> 00:38:38,233
I'm tired.

736
00:38:42,612 --> 00:38:45,907
Ever since I started working

737
00:38:45,990 --> 00:38:48,159
I've always had to prove myself.

738
00:38:51,162 --> 00:38:54,290
I ended up doing crazy things...

739
00:38:55,625 --> 00:38:57,210
just so people
would take me seriously.

740
00:39:03,842 --> 00:39:06,302
How do I not leave SAM now, Camille?

741
00:39:08,513 --> 00:39:10,932
This is my biggest mistake ever.

742
00:39:11,641 --> 00:39:12,725
Come on now.

743
00:39:13,726 --> 00:39:16,229
I'd rather mess up here
than anywhere else.

744
00:39:17,480 --> 00:39:19,899
I'm so far from my real home

745
00:39:19,983 --> 00:39:21,943
but SAM is my home and family here.

746
00:39:22,026 --> 00:39:23,695
Not just because of Sir Matthew.

747
00:39:24,946 --> 00:39:26,030
It's because of you guys.

748
00:39:29,659 --> 00:39:32,453
If I mess up
and Ms. Andrea screams at me?

749
00:39:33,079 --> 00:39:36,833
I know you guys care enough about me

750
00:39:36,916 --> 00:39:39,794
to give me a chance
to make up for it.

751
00:39:44,090 --> 00:39:45,216
Sorry, Camille.

752
00:39:50,054 --> 00:39:51,180
Did you tell him?

753
00:39:53,224 --> 00:39:54,309
Tell me what?

754
00:39:58,980 --> 00:40:00,189
Camille's right.

755
00:40:00,732 --> 00:40:02,317
No one has to know.

756
00:40:03,026 --> 00:40:05,111
You only have to tell them one thing.

757
00:40:06,279 --> 00:40:07,280
Huh?

758
00:40:09,449 --> 00:40:11,868
[upbeat music]

759
00:40:11,951 --> 00:40:13,036
Oh, man.

760
00:40:13,661 --> 00:40:15,413
I've messed up a lot of times.

761
00:40:16,497 --> 00:40:20,001
But I don't dwell on my mistakes.

762
00:40:21,419 --> 00:40:22,420
I fix them

763
00:40:23,463 --> 00:40:24,464
erase them

764
00:40:25,256 --> 00:40:26,466
and make them all right.

765
00:40:27,926 --> 00:40:29,469
[in English] Tomorrow is another day.

766
00:40:30,637 --> 00:40:33,389
Tomorrow is another chance
to make things right.

767
00:40:35,433 --> 00:40:37,101
[in Filipino] I checked everything.

768
00:40:37,936 --> 00:40:39,562
There is no one source.

769
00:40:39,854 --> 00:40:40,939
There is no leak.

770
00:40:41,439 --> 00:40:43,316
There are too many people involved.

771
00:40:43,399 --> 00:40:45,735
The gossips are just so good
at what they do.

772
00:40:46,277 --> 00:40:49,906
They're so good at weaving
all the information into stories.

773
00:40:49,989 --> 00:40:53,785
Instead of looking
for the source of the leaks

774
00:40:53,868 --> 00:40:59,123
we should just help our artists
deal with the rumors.

775
00:40:59,207 --> 00:41:01,000
We do that so well.

776
00:41:01,084 --> 00:41:04,253
We've done it before for Ms. Laurice.

777
00:41:04,337 --> 00:41:09,092
Let's reclaim social media
and use it to our advantage.

778
00:41:09,175 --> 00:41:10,259
Good!

779
00:41:11,010 --> 00:41:12,095
Next question.

780
00:41:13,471 --> 00:41:15,807
Throughout your stay in SAM

781
00:41:16,432 --> 00:41:19,268
what has been
your biggest challenge so far?

782
00:41:19,686 --> 00:41:21,270
I just can't say no to anything.

783
00:41:21,604 --> 00:41:26,317
I'm always grumpy when I'm tired
or when there's too much work to do.

784
00:41:26,734 --> 00:41:30,071
No matter how tough it is.

785
00:41:30,154 --> 00:41:32,240
But no matter how mean I get,
I make sure I'm pretty.

786
00:41:32,323 --> 00:41:33,700
Ms. Andrea.

787
00:41:35,159 --> 00:41:38,496
I don't know her too well yet

788
00:41:38,579 --> 00:41:40,289
so I make a lot of mistakes.

789
00:41:40,373 --> 00:41:43,209
[in English] What do you think
are your best assets?

790
00:41:43,292 --> 00:41:45,128
[in Filipino] I love my talents.

791
00:41:45,211 --> 00:41:46,629
I'm a good teacher.

792
00:41:46,713 --> 00:41:49,090
I'll do anything for them.

793
00:41:49,173 --> 00:41:54,053
An ex-coworker said to me...

794
00:41:54,762 --> 00:41:58,016
"Why should I mentor you?
Nobody taught me when I started."

795
00:41:58,641 --> 00:42:00,935
I got out of there real fast.

796
00:42:01,936 --> 00:42:04,564
Here in SAM, we're a family.

797
00:42:05,314 --> 00:42:08,026
If one of us messes up,
it's everybody's mistake.

798
00:42:09,277 --> 00:42:13,114
I'm here to teach my family
how not to mess up.

799
00:42:13,197 --> 00:42:15,408
[in English] And I thank you.

800
00:42:16,159 --> 00:42:18,286
[in Filipino]
Are they grilling Chin? How is he?

801
00:42:18,369 --> 00:42:20,288
I'm sure he's fine, don't worry.

802
00:42:21,748 --> 00:42:23,583
- [Noemi] Well?
- He's alive, thank god.

803
00:42:25,543 --> 00:42:26,586
I think I did okay.

804
00:42:26,669 --> 00:42:27,837
It's all good.

805
00:42:31,215 --> 00:42:33,468
Thank you, girls.

806
00:42:34,093 --> 00:42:36,179
Thank you. I'm really sorry.

807
00:42:36,262 --> 00:42:37,889
It won't happen again. I promise.

808
00:42:37,972 --> 00:42:39,724
- Mm...
- Mm-hm.

809
00:42:39,807 --> 00:42:41,059
Group hug!

810
00:42:41,142 --> 00:42:43,227
[all giggle]

811
00:42:43,728 --> 00:42:45,646
[announcer in English]
Presenting the talented nominees

812
00:42:45,730 --> 00:42:49,692
for this year's highly anticipated
Screen Spirit Awards.

813
00:42:50,109 --> 00:42:52,987
This year's nominees
for the Screen Spirit Awards

814
00:42:53,071 --> 00:42:54,322
Best Actor are...

815
00:42:54,614 --> 00:42:56,282
Sir Roderick!

816
00:42:56,365 --> 00:42:57,992
[in Filipino]
They're announcing the nominees!

817
00:42:58,076 --> 00:43:00,161
[announcer in English]
Joel Torre for Celebes.

818
00:43:01,037 --> 00:43:03,623
Rob Gomez for When Love Calls.

819
00:43:04,123 --> 00:43:06,709
And Roderick Paulate
for The Lonely One!

820
00:43:06,793 --> 00:43:08,127
Not really news when it's a given.

821
00:43:08,211 --> 00:43:09,545
- Congrats, sir!
- Thank you!

822
00:43:09,629 --> 00:43:13,716
The nominees for the Screen Spirit
Awards for Best Actress are

823
00:43:14,092 --> 00:43:16,427
Lotlot de Leon for The Sacrifice.

824
00:43:17,178 --> 00:43:19,597
Maricel Soriano for For Alida.

825
00:43:20,014 --> 00:43:21,015
- Thank you!
- Mm.

826
00:43:22,016 --> 00:43:24,143
Snooky Serna for Sabel's Secret.

827
00:43:25,561 --> 00:43:28,272
And Lynette Marie Vicencio
for Amihan and I.

828
00:43:28,940 --> 00:43:30,024
[Camille] Congratulations, ma'am!

829
00:43:30,691 --> 00:43:32,235
Who's that other nominee?

830
00:43:32,860 --> 00:43:35,988
I knew it! You were only listening
for your own name.

831
00:43:36,906 --> 00:43:39,117
That one has nothing on you two.

832
00:43:39,575 --> 00:43:42,120
That's Willy Wu's latest girl!

833
00:43:42,578 --> 00:43:43,788
The producer?

834
00:43:43,871 --> 00:43:44,872
The producer!

835
00:43:44,956 --> 00:43:47,125
And the producer of all of her films.

836
00:43:47,208 --> 00:43:48,209
So that's why.

837
00:43:48,292 --> 00:43:50,878
Mother Aleta's Last Wish
is nominated for Best Picture.

838
00:43:50,962 --> 00:43:52,255
SAM co-produced that.

839
00:43:52,338 --> 00:43:53,381
Wow.

840
00:43:53,464 --> 00:43:55,466
SAM has a lot of nominees.

841
00:43:55,883 --> 00:43:57,093
Too bad you're closing shop soon.

842
00:43:57,885 --> 00:43:59,887
[Roderick] Okay, back to work!

843
00:44:00,304 --> 00:44:02,598
Hey, what's this light doing here?
Take it out!

844
00:44:02,682 --> 00:44:05,309
Looks like my Aunt Metring
will get a job soon.

845
00:44:06,018 --> 00:44:10,356
What is SAM doing
about all these rumors?

846
00:44:10,439 --> 00:44:11,566
What are you doing about this?

847
00:44:11,899 --> 00:44:13,693
Yeah, what's being done?

848
00:44:14,402 --> 00:44:16,612
I think the director needs you
on the set.

849
00:44:17,113 --> 00:44:18,698
Evasive maneuvers, huh?

850
00:44:19,782 --> 00:44:21,325
- Whatever!
- It was just a simple question.

851
00:44:22,618 --> 00:44:24,203
[Andrea] Yes, Zsa Zsa, don't worry.

852
00:44:24,287 --> 00:44:27,748
Our RMs are doing their jobs.

853
00:44:28,207 --> 00:44:30,126
Yeah. By tomorrow, I promise you

854
00:44:30,543 --> 00:44:32,920
that video will be gone from YouTube.

855
00:44:33,880 --> 00:44:35,965
I'll update you, okay? Bye.

856
00:44:36,257 --> 00:44:37,592
Her decision's final.

857
00:44:39,343 --> 00:44:40,928
She's leaving us.

858
00:44:42,013 --> 00:44:43,014
[Gab] And Brandon?

859
00:44:43,848 --> 00:44:45,600
He'll talk it over with the missus.

860
00:44:47,059 --> 00:44:49,520
- You told him not to believe Paul?
- Yeah.

861
00:44:49,604 --> 00:44:51,689
Missus? They were just fighting.

862
00:44:51,772 --> 00:44:52,773
But this is about money.

863
00:44:53,774 --> 00:44:54,901
That's the only time they'll talk.

864
00:44:54,984 --> 00:44:57,278
Money, they agree on.

865
00:44:57,862 --> 00:44:58,863
Speaking of money

866
00:44:59,614 --> 00:45:00,656
I don't have any.

867
00:45:00,740 --> 00:45:01,782
That's not news.

868
00:45:02,241 --> 00:45:05,453
That's all I have
and it won't even cover my share.

869
00:45:06,287 --> 00:45:07,330
Any word from the bank?

870
00:45:09,790 --> 00:45:10,791
Nothing.

871
00:45:11,042 --> 00:45:12,126
They said they'd call.

872
00:45:13,085 --> 00:45:16,380
But you know, guys, we really have
to check on SAM's assets

873
00:45:17,048 --> 00:45:18,466
or we'll never hear from the bank.

874
00:45:19,050 --> 00:45:21,093
At least our application is there.

875
00:45:24,138 --> 00:45:25,139
Oh?

876
00:45:25,223 --> 00:45:28,226
Where's the energy
and the optimism, boys?

877
00:45:29,227 --> 00:45:30,811
Where's our mantra?

878
00:45:30,895 --> 00:45:33,731
"We own SAM, SAM is ours!"

879
00:45:35,233 --> 00:45:36,234
Right?

880
00:45:38,194 --> 00:45:39,237
"Right, Andrea?"

881
00:45:39,320 --> 00:45:41,239
- "Yes, SAM is ours."
- [knocks on door]

882
00:45:42,198 --> 00:45:43,199
[Andrea] Come in.

883
00:45:43,950 --> 00:45:46,327
There's someone here to see you.

884
00:45:46,953 --> 00:45:48,079
No appointment?

885
00:45:48,162 --> 00:45:49,163
[Sofie] No.

886
00:45:50,289 --> 00:45:53,167
Oh, well, might as well see them.

887
00:45:53,251 --> 00:45:55,086
Could be a future client.

888
00:45:55,169 --> 00:45:56,587
- [grunts]
- Let's go.

889
00:45:57,255 --> 00:45:59,340
You should stay here, Sir Gab.

890
00:45:59,799 --> 00:46:01,217
- Wait, why?
- Why?

891
00:46:03,219 --> 00:46:05,805
It's Frank Villacin, he's downstairs.

892
00:46:05,888 --> 00:46:07,848
[tense music]

893
00:46:07,932 --> 00:46:09,141
I can't see him.

894
00:46:09,809 --> 00:46:11,394
I know. We'll stay here.

895
00:46:14,730 --> 00:46:16,983
Just sit. Sit down.

896
00:46:24,865 --> 00:46:26,575
- [clears throat]
- Oh.

897
00:46:28,244 --> 00:46:29,370
[Frank] Oh?

898
00:46:30,955 --> 00:46:32,915
Aren't there three of you?
Where's the other one?

899
00:46:38,212 --> 00:46:39,213
[in English] I'm sorry

900
00:46:39,755 --> 00:46:40,756
no smoking.

901
00:46:41,173 --> 00:46:42,174
No smoking.

902
00:46:42,967 --> 00:46:44,051
[in Filipino] Even for visitors?

903
00:46:45,052 --> 00:46:46,053
Yes.

904
00:46:47,013 --> 00:46:50,683
These ceiling leaks are really bad.

905
00:46:51,434 --> 00:46:52,935
We can file a complaint.

906
00:46:53,561 --> 00:46:55,354
I know the City Engineer.

907
00:46:55,438 --> 00:46:58,107
He can assess the damage
and we can sue the building owners.

908
00:46:58,357 --> 00:47:00,901
I send him all the complainants
on my show.

909
00:47:02,194 --> 00:47:04,447
[gasps] Sorry, that's broken.

910
00:47:06,949 --> 00:47:09,410
[Andrea in English]
So what do you want, Mr. Villacin?

911
00:47:09,493 --> 00:47:10,494
[in Filipino] Call me Frank.

912
00:47:13,205 --> 00:47:15,416
[in English]
Okay, to make a long story short

913
00:47:16,709 --> 00:47:20,921
I want Shine Artist Management...

914
00:47:22,506 --> 00:47:23,591
to manage me.

915
00:47:24,508 --> 00:47:25,968
Is this some kind of a joke?

916
00:47:27,345 --> 00:47:28,387
[Frank] As you may know

917
00:47:29,430 --> 00:47:31,307
I'm running for public office again.

918
00:47:32,767 --> 00:47:34,518
But that's still six years away.

919
00:47:34,602 --> 00:47:36,228
And I want to be prepared.

920
00:47:36,812 --> 00:47:38,939
I want to start now.

921
00:47:39,357 --> 00:47:41,942
Frank You is a top-rater.

922
00:47:42,443 --> 00:47:46,655
[in Filipino] I have many followers
lining up for help at my office.

923
00:47:46,739 --> 00:47:48,783
People come to me for help.

924
00:47:49,867 --> 00:47:51,702
And I help all of them.

925
00:47:51,786 --> 00:47:53,079
Oh, yeah.

926
00:47:53,162 --> 00:47:55,456
But not before you make them fight.

927
00:47:55,539 --> 00:47:59,377
That is what my viewers
and listeners want.

928
00:48:00,127 --> 00:48:01,295
[in English] We're not publicists.

929
00:48:02,046 --> 00:48:04,590
[in Filipino]
Our job is managing talents.

930
00:48:04,673 --> 00:48:06,133
[in English] But you know what to do.

931
00:48:07,093 --> 00:48:08,928
And you have the machinery.

932
00:48:12,181 --> 00:48:14,016
[in Filipino] Sorry, that's expired.

933
00:48:19,688 --> 00:48:21,232
Does anything still work in here?

934
00:48:23,692 --> 00:48:24,819
You guys are good.

935
00:48:26,529 --> 00:48:27,863
That thing with Rob Gomez?

936
00:48:28,572 --> 00:48:30,574
You did a good job
of keeping that under wraps.

937
00:48:32,284 --> 00:48:33,411
[in English] How dare you.

938
00:48:33,994 --> 00:48:34,995
[in Filipino] Me?

939
00:48:35,621 --> 00:48:37,289
I just got that off...

940
00:48:38,707 --> 00:48:40,126
of Cristy's vlog.

941
00:48:40,626 --> 00:48:41,669
So...

942
00:48:43,087 --> 00:48:44,797
[in English] I don't know
what you're talking about.

943
00:48:47,842 --> 00:48:48,926
[in Filipino] But if I did...

944
00:48:50,553 --> 00:48:51,679
have something to do with that...

945
00:48:55,349 --> 00:48:56,976
It's in the past.

946
00:48:57,476 --> 00:48:58,978
We're even, and life goes on.

947
00:49:02,440 --> 00:49:04,567
Let me sweeten the deal.

948
00:49:08,696 --> 00:49:11,782
[in English] Agree to my terms...

949
00:49:13,742 --> 00:49:15,161
and I'll pay you good money.

950
00:49:18,164 --> 00:49:19,290
Why SAM?

951
00:49:20,082 --> 00:49:21,125
Why us?

952
00:49:21,500 --> 00:49:22,585
Because you're the best.

953
00:49:24,753 --> 00:49:27,882
And that's the only kind
I want on my team.

954
00:49:28,757 --> 00:49:30,468
[in Filipino] And I want to serve.

955
00:49:32,094 --> 00:49:33,304
[in English] I can serve you.

956
00:49:35,347 --> 00:49:36,474
[in Filipino] I may just be...

957
00:49:38,100 --> 00:49:40,895
the help you need to keep SAM afloat.

958
00:49:42,438 --> 00:49:45,191
Actually, I am all you need.

959
00:49:48,319 --> 00:49:49,653
[in English] You know, um...

960
00:49:50,779 --> 00:49:52,615
I'm sorry, Mr. Villacin.

961
00:49:53,657 --> 00:49:55,201
[Matthew] You'll have to go
somewhere else.

962
00:49:55,284 --> 00:49:56,452
We here at SAM...

963
00:49:56,535 --> 00:49:57,786
We'll talk about it.

964
00:49:59,413 --> 00:50:00,456
We'll get back to you.

965
00:50:01,373 --> 00:50:04,418
There's no way I'm managing
the career of that criminal!

966
00:50:04,793 --> 00:50:06,837
[in Filipino]
Andrea, he's a criminal.

967
00:50:06,921 --> 00:50:07,963
[Gab] That's all he is!

968
00:50:08,631 --> 00:50:10,007
It was just a thought.

969
00:50:10,090 --> 00:50:11,300
We don't have to do it.

970
00:50:11,383 --> 00:50:14,887
Or I can manage him myself,
you don't have to be involved.

971
00:50:14,970 --> 00:50:16,472
[in English] That's crazy, Andrea!

972
00:50:16,805 --> 00:50:18,557
Yes, thank you very much!

973
00:50:18,641 --> 00:50:19,767
That is crazy!

974
00:50:20,100 --> 00:50:21,101
You were there.

975
00:50:21,810 --> 00:50:23,229
[in Filipino]
You saw what he did to Rob!

976
00:50:23,979 --> 00:50:25,981
[suspenseful music]

977
00:50:40,246 --> 00:50:44,041
[inaudible dialogue]

978
00:50:54,677 --> 00:50:56,679
[suspenseful music intensifies]

979
00:51:05,688 --> 00:51:07,940
[sobbing]

980
00:51:12,069 --> 00:51:14,071
[panting]

981
00:51:31,839 --> 00:51:32,840
Where's Rob?

982
00:51:40,431 --> 00:51:41,432
[Rob] Chin...

983
00:51:41,890 --> 00:51:42,975
Chin!

984
00:51:44,018 --> 00:51:45,019
Chin!

985
00:51:45,603 --> 00:51:46,604
Chin!

986
00:51:53,360 --> 00:51:55,696
[sobbing]

987
00:51:59,908 --> 00:52:01,577
No! Poor Rob.

988
00:52:02,161 --> 00:52:03,245
I can't do a thing for him.

989
00:52:03,621 --> 00:52:05,623
- And Andrea is talking crazy.
- Sir Gab.

990
00:52:06,582 --> 00:52:07,583
Sir Gab.

991
00:52:08,626 --> 00:52:09,627
Gabriel.

992
00:52:12,504 --> 00:52:13,756
[Sofie] Rob is young.

993
00:52:15,424 --> 00:52:16,759
He'll get over it.

994
00:52:18,052 --> 00:52:19,053
Okay?

995
00:52:19,720 --> 00:52:21,096
And this is Rob.

996
00:52:22,556 --> 00:52:25,934
He knows what's important.

997
00:52:26,018 --> 00:52:27,311
His family is important.

998
00:52:29,021 --> 00:52:31,690
He'll get through this for them.

999
00:52:31,774 --> 00:52:33,651
And he has his SAM family.

1000
00:52:35,694 --> 00:52:38,155
He has us. He has you.

1001
00:52:39,323 --> 00:52:42,451
He has Gabriel who takes care of him.

1002
00:52:42,534 --> 00:52:45,412
The Gabriel who is always there
for his talents.

1003
00:52:48,707 --> 00:52:50,125
He'll get through this.

1004
00:52:51,001 --> 00:52:52,127
He will never be alone.

1005
00:52:53,587 --> 00:52:54,588
Okay?

1006
00:52:58,384 --> 00:52:59,718
What if he leaves SAM?

1007
00:53:02,262 --> 00:53:03,514
Don't think that way.

1008
00:53:05,808 --> 00:53:07,476
But if it happens...

1009
00:53:09,853 --> 00:53:11,522
we move on.

1010
00:53:13,273 --> 00:53:14,775
We have no choice.

1011
00:53:38,132 --> 00:53:39,133
What is it?

1012
00:53:42,052 --> 00:53:43,971
Are you sure you wanna be an actor?

1013
00:53:47,975 --> 00:53:49,518
I think you'll make a great manager.

1014
00:53:50,769 --> 00:53:51,770
What?

1015
00:53:51,854 --> 00:53:53,188
[chuckles]

1016
00:53:53,272 --> 00:53:54,314
Me?

1017
00:54:06,827 --> 00:54:07,870
If it were just me...

1018
00:54:09,496 --> 00:54:10,998
this would be nothing.

1019
00:54:13,250 --> 00:54:14,752
But I have a family to think of.

1020
00:54:16,462 --> 00:54:17,838
Then you can do this, right?

1021
00:54:17,921 --> 00:54:19,047
For your family.

1022
00:54:22,509 --> 00:54:23,594
[exhales sharply]

1023
00:54:25,596 --> 00:54:27,389
Will you really quit acting?

1024
00:54:31,310 --> 00:54:33,270
Maybe I can go back to the province.

1025
00:54:35,314 --> 00:54:36,690
Taxes are way lower there.

1026
00:54:37,733 --> 00:54:38,734
[chuckles]

1027
00:54:41,987 --> 00:54:42,988
You know, Chin...

1028
00:54:44,156 --> 00:54:46,074
I made one small mistake...

1029
00:54:47,993 --> 00:54:49,453
and I'm ruined forever.

1030
00:54:57,544 --> 00:55:00,422
Hey, why are you crying too?

1031
00:55:06,762 --> 00:55:08,597
I made a mistake too.

1032
00:55:10,432 --> 00:55:13,393
I did you wrong,
but I didn't mean to.

1033
00:55:13,477 --> 00:55:15,896
- I'm so sorry.
- Chin...

1034
00:55:16,647 --> 00:55:19,149
I can't imagine you doing any wrong.

1035
00:55:19,233 --> 00:55:22,110
You don't understand.

1036
00:55:22,861 --> 00:55:24,988
If you knew what I've done and said.

1037
00:55:25,072 --> 00:55:26,365
Chin.

1038
00:55:30,327 --> 00:55:31,370
Whatever it is...

1039
00:55:34,456 --> 00:55:35,499
You can forget about it.

1040
00:55:37,751 --> 00:55:39,670
Everything you've done for me...

1041
00:55:42,047 --> 00:55:43,715
trumps anything wrong you did.

1042
00:55:46,426 --> 00:55:47,761
Thank you.

1043
00:55:49,596 --> 00:55:50,597
Come here.

1044
00:55:59,940 --> 00:56:02,442
[in English] Well, look who's here.

1045
00:56:03,360 --> 00:56:04,361
[in Filipino] How are you?

1046
00:56:07,489 --> 00:56:08,782
[in English] Not that I care.

1047
00:56:10,492 --> 00:56:12,119
[in Filipino]
That's just my standard greeting.

1048
00:56:13,120 --> 00:56:16,331
But I'm a decent woman,
so I'll ask you to sit.

1049
00:56:18,500 --> 00:56:19,710
[Aleta in English] Thank you, Helen.

1050
00:56:25,716 --> 00:56:26,717
Helen.

1051
00:56:27,509 --> 00:56:30,012
[in Filipino] We're too old to be
pulling each other's hair, aren't we?

1052
00:56:31,597 --> 00:56:32,598
[scoffs]

1053
00:56:32,973 --> 00:56:33,974
Well...

1054
00:56:35,851 --> 00:56:38,103
Don't you have questions for me?

1055
00:56:39,438 --> 00:56:41,023
About me and Samuel?

1056
00:56:42,441 --> 00:56:43,442
Nothing.

1057
00:56:43,942 --> 00:56:45,235
I no longer care about that.

1058
00:56:46,236 --> 00:56:47,529
[in English] It's all in the past.

1059
00:56:50,866 --> 00:56:53,035
All the memories I have with Samuel

1060
00:56:53,118 --> 00:56:54,119
include you.

1061
00:56:56,580 --> 00:56:58,415
[in Filipino]
Why would I want to relive that?

1062
00:57:00,208 --> 00:57:04,004
He's the one who left me, Helen.

1063
00:57:04,671 --> 00:57:06,006
[in English] I don't believe you.

1064
00:57:06,924 --> 00:57:10,636
He would've left me for you
the minute he had a chance.

1065
00:57:11,929 --> 00:57:13,555
[in Filipino] And he had his chances.

1066
00:57:14,514 --> 00:57:15,891
But he didn't leave you.

1067
00:57:18,143 --> 00:57:22,272
It's because he loved you,
that's why he stayed.

1068
00:57:26,526 --> 00:57:28,236
This is good news, right?

1069
00:57:29,404 --> 00:57:30,530
I mean

1070
00:57:30,614 --> 00:57:32,115
if they're asking us for all this

1071
00:57:32,199 --> 00:57:36,870
maybe they're considering
granting us the loan?

1072
00:57:36,954 --> 00:57:38,163
- Mm-hm.
- Right?

1073
00:57:40,540 --> 00:57:42,542
- [knocks on door]
- [sighs] Come in.

1074
00:57:43,919 --> 00:57:46,380
Ms. Andrea, this just came in.

1075
00:57:47,506 --> 00:57:48,507
Thank you.

1076
00:57:48,590 --> 00:57:51,051
Camille, can you call everyone?

1077
00:57:51,134 --> 00:57:52,636
- [Camille] Okay, ma'am.
- [Andrea] Thank you.

1078
00:57:53,387 --> 00:57:54,388
Wait.

1079
00:57:54,763 --> 00:57:55,764
Wait.

1080
00:57:56,264 --> 00:57:58,141
We're making another announcement?

1081
00:57:59,267 --> 00:58:02,104
Why should we if we can't buy SAM?

1082
00:58:02,187 --> 00:58:03,188
Why not?

1083
00:58:03,939 --> 00:58:04,982
We still have a week.

1084
00:58:05,065 --> 00:58:06,316
Anything can happen.

1085
00:58:06,400 --> 00:58:07,401
Exactly.

1086
00:58:07,609 --> 00:58:08,610
Matty's right.

1087
00:58:09,069 --> 00:58:10,529
Anything can happen.

1088
00:58:10,612 --> 00:58:12,072
With that being said

1089
00:58:12,155 --> 00:58:16,243
I think you should handle
all the paperwork and requirements.

1090
00:58:16,868 --> 00:58:20,789
You know how this goes,
you'll get it done properly.

1091
00:58:22,958 --> 00:58:24,501
[sighs] This isn't over yet.

1092
00:58:24,918 --> 00:58:26,545
We're not going down without a fight.

1093
00:58:30,048 --> 00:58:31,299
[Andrea] As you all know

1094
00:58:31,925 --> 00:58:34,928
SAM is nominated in many categories
in the Screen Spirit Awards.

1095
00:58:35,220 --> 00:58:38,765
So me, Gab, and Matt
have decided to make it a party!

1096
00:58:38,849 --> 00:58:41,643
[all cheer]

1097
00:58:41,727 --> 00:58:45,480
And just so we're clear,
everyone is attending!

1098
00:58:45,564 --> 00:58:47,315
[screams]

1099
00:58:47,399 --> 00:58:48,900
Including me?

1100
00:58:48,984 --> 00:58:52,029
[overlapping excited chatter]

1101
00:58:53,280 --> 00:58:55,365
- Okay, hold on.
- [Camille] Chin.

1102
00:58:55,449 --> 00:58:57,659
- Here are the invites.
- There we go!

1103
00:58:57,743 --> 00:58:59,953
Please take one and pass it around.

1104
00:59:00,037 --> 00:59:01,913
[overlapping chatter]

1105
00:59:01,997 --> 00:59:02,998
[Andrea] Kids...

1106
00:59:04,249 --> 00:59:05,625
...take care.

1107
00:59:05,709 --> 00:59:07,961
- See you tomorrow.
- I'm an actor!

1108
00:59:08,378 --> 00:59:09,671
[Matthew] Hey, wait!

1109
00:59:10,088 --> 00:59:11,214
Come back, everyone.

1110
00:59:12,632 --> 00:59:13,633
Come back.

1111
00:59:14,509 --> 00:59:17,888
- We owe you one last thing.
- Oh, right.

1112
00:59:23,185 --> 00:59:24,603
[Andrea] If it's up to you...

1113
00:59:25,103 --> 00:59:26,730
If you were to make a choice...

1114
00:59:27,147 --> 00:59:29,066
Aside from yourself

1115
00:59:29,900 --> 00:59:32,402
who do you think should be

1116
00:59:33,070 --> 00:59:34,529
the new junior manager?

1117
00:59:37,741 --> 00:59:38,992
Right! We've decided.

1118
00:59:40,786 --> 00:59:43,955
- And after careful deliberation...
- Mm-hm.

1119
00:59:45,332 --> 00:59:46,500
Please welcome

1120
00:59:47,084 --> 00:59:49,920
your newest junior manager...

1121
00:59:51,046 --> 00:59:52,297
Um...

1122
00:59:57,803 --> 00:59:59,179
[drum rolls]

1123
00:59:59,262 --> 01:00:00,305
Noemi!

1124
01:00:00,388 --> 01:00:02,390
[all cheering]

1125
01:00:06,895 --> 01:00:08,855
[indistinct dialogue over cell phone]

1126
01:00:08,939 --> 01:00:10,649
Shh, listen!

1127
01:00:13,819 --> 01:00:16,571
[congressman] ...70 Yes, 11 No.

1128
01:00:17,197 --> 01:00:19,324
Two inhibited, one abstained.

1129
01:00:21,159 --> 01:00:23,120
The resolution to deny ABS-CBN's

1130
01:00:23,203 --> 01:00:25,247
franchise application
is hereby adopted...

1131
01:00:26,248 --> 01:00:28,083
Pursuant to Section 49 of the...

1132
01:00:29,167 --> 01:00:31,795
What? What did they just do?

1133
01:00:33,046 --> 01:00:35,632
- [cell phone ringing]
- [overlapping clamor]

1134
01:00:36,341 --> 01:00:38,176
Yeah, Zsa Zsa, I know...

1135
01:00:38,260 --> 01:00:40,011
[Gab] Yeah, we just heard it.

1136
01:00:41,721 --> 01:00:43,932
[Matthew] We just heard.
Breaking news.

1137
01:00:44,766 --> 01:00:46,268
Who voted?

1138
01:00:47,269 --> 01:00:48,770
[Chin shrieks]

1139
01:00:48,854 --> 01:00:49,855
[Gab] I'll call you back.

1140
01:00:49,938 --> 01:00:51,064
- [Andrea] Hold on.
- [Chin] Wait.

1141
01:00:51,148 --> 01:00:52,983
- [Camille] I'm very sorry.
- [Chin] I'll get a lamp.

1142
01:00:53,066 --> 01:00:54,609
- [Matthew] Don't hang up.
- [Gab] Where's Deo?

1143
01:00:54,693 --> 01:00:56,611
- [Camille] We lost power.
- [Andrea] What happened?

1144
01:00:56,695 --> 01:00:59,322
[overlapping chatter]

1145
01:00:59,865 --> 01:01:01,116
[Gab] Hey, look.

1146
01:01:01,992 --> 01:01:04,244
Is it just us having a power outage?

1147
01:01:04,327 --> 01:01:05,871
- Huh?
- Are you serious?

1148
01:01:07,789 --> 01:01:09,791
- [Andrea] What?
- It's just us.

1149
01:01:09,875 --> 01:01:10,876
Yeah.

1150
01:01:12,711 --> 01:01:13,712
What's happening?

1151
01:01:17,674 --> 01:01:18,800
Darn it.

1152
01:01:23,555 --> 01:01:25,557
[closing theme music]
